  "name": "Civil engineering",
  "section": "F",
  "summary": "Civil engineering groups link AI to demand through data-centre campuses, power generation, transmission, substations and fibre built for hyperscalers and for utilities facing load growth. Own use covers BIM and digital twins, machine control and autonomous earthmoving, drone surveys, AI-based scheduling and bid-risk tools, tunnelling automation and computer-vision safety. Concession and road operators add AI inspection of pavements and structures, traffic prediction, camera-based tolling and dynamic pricing; labour shortages and power availability are the constraint themes.",
